    "created_at": "2025-11-10T05:05:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-10T05:05:37Z",
    "body": "I think a risk of a requirement that `table` elements must have accessible names is that there will be more bogus accessible names added to satisfy conformance checkers. Since there are also pages that misuse `table` elements for layout purposes, having such tables start to use accessible names could impact the heuristic to detect data tables vs layout tables, which would be bad for accessibility.\n\nSo I think HTML shouldn't add this requirement. Given the above, maybe ARIA also shouldn't have this requirement for `table`?",
